We have,
$f(x)=\frac{(x+1) \sinh x}{e^{2 x} \tan x}=(x+1) \sinh x e^{-2 x} \cot x\begin{array}{r}\therefore f^{\prime}(x)=\sinh x e^{-2 x} \cot x+(x+1) \cosh x e^{-2 x} \cot x \\ +(x+1) \sinh x e^{-2 x}(-2) \cot x \\ +(x+1) \sinh x e^{-2 x}\left(-\operatorname{coscc}^2 x\right)\end{array}
$\begin{aligned} & \Rightarrow f^{\prime}(x)=(x+1) \sinh x^{-2 x} \cot x \\ & \quad\left[\frac{1}{x+1}+\operatorname{coth} x-2-\frac{\operatorname{cosec}^2 x}{\cot x}\right] \\ & \Rightarrow f^{\prime}(x)=f(x)\left[\frac{1}{x+1}+\operatorname{coth} x-2-\frac{\sin x}{\sin ^2 x \cos x}\right]\end{aligned}\Rightarrow \frac{f^{\prime}(x)}{f(x)}=\frac{1}{x+1}+\operatorname{coth} x-2-2 \operatorname{cosec} 2 x\therefore \quad g(x)=-2(1+\operatorname{cosec} 2 x)

We have,
$\begin{array}{r}\frac{x^4+3 x+1}{(x+1)^2(x-1)}=A x+B+\frac{C}{x+1}+\frac{D}{(x+1)^2}+\frac{E}{x-1} \\ \Rightarrow x^4+3 x+1=A x(x+1)^2(x-1)+B(x+1)^2(x-1) \\ \quad+C(x+1)(x-1)+D(x-1)+E(x+1)^2 \\ \Rightarrow x^4+3 x+1=A x\left(x^3+x^2-x-1\right) \\ +B\left(x^3-1 x^2-x-1\right)+C\left(x^2-1\right) \\ \quad+D(x-1)+E\left(x^2+2 x+1\right) \\ \Rightarrow x^4+3 x+1=A x^4+(A+B) x^3 \\ +(-A+B+C+E) x^2+(-A-B+D+2 E) x \\ +(-B-C-D+E)\end{array}
$\begin{aligned} A & =1 \\ A+B & =0 \\ -A+B+C+E & =0 \\ -A-B+D+2 E & =3 \\ -B-C-D+E & =1\end{aligned}\therefore \quad A=1, B=-1, C=\frac{+3}{4}, D=\frac{1}{2}, E=\frac{5}{4}\begin{gathered}\therefore \quad A+B+C+D+E=1-1+\frac{3}{4}+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{5}{4} \\ =\frac{+3+2+5}{4}=\frac{10}{4}=\frac{5}{2} .\end{gathered}

